Cache the generated zoxide init next to the other caches, never next to the code.

`_initZoxide` writes a generated `zoxide_init_cache.py` and imports it on later
starts, which saves compiling the output of `zoxide init xonsh` every time. It
picks the directory from `$XDG_CACHE_HOME` -- but only when that variable is
set, and falls back to its own installed package directory when it is not.

$XDG_CACHE_HOME is unset on most systems: the basedir spec defines it as
*optional* with a default of `$HOME/.cache`, so a program is meant to apply
that default rather than treat "unset" as "no cache directory". Falling back to
the install directory is wrong on any read-only installation, and a Nix store
path is exactly that -- the first import raises
`OSError: [Errno 30] Read-only file system`, and the xontrib never loads.

So: apply the spec's own default. `~/.cache/zoxide/` on a normal system, and
`$XDG_CACHE_HOME/zoxide/` still wins where it is set, which is unchanged
behaviour for anyone who has it.

Not Nix-specific, and worth sending upstream:
https://github.com/dyuri/xontrib-zoxide

--- a/xontrib/zoxide/zoxide.py
+++ b/xontrib/zoxide/zoxide.py
@@ -17,11 +17,9 @@
     f.write(zoxide_init)
 
 def  _initZoxide():
-  if cache_home := os.environ.get("XDG_CACHE_HOME"):
-    z_cache_path = Path(cache_home).expanduser() / "zoxide" / _cache_name
-    z_cache_path.parent.mkdir(exist_ok=True, parents=True)
-  else:
-    z_cache_path	= Path(os.path.dirname(__file__)).parent / _cache_name
+  cache_home = os.environ.get("XDG_CACHE_HOME") or "~/.cache"
+  z_cache_path = Path(cache_home).expanduser() / "zoxide" / _cache_name
+  z_cache_path.parent.mkdir(exist_ok=True, parents=True)
   sys.path.append(str(z_cache_path.parent))
 
   zoxide_init_proc	= subprocess.run(["zoxide",'init','xonsh'],capture_output=True)
